    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA rare opportunity to acquire a charming two-bedroom end-of-terrace home occupying an enviable position at the end of a quiet cul-de-sac, set on a generous site with extensive gardens, side access and exceptional scope to extend and remodel, subject to planning permission.\n\nNo. 16 is a home of enormous potential, ideally suited to purchasers seeking a home they can modernise and transform to their own specification. While the accommodation is well maintained and retains much of its original character, the true appeal lies in the opportunity to create a significantly larger home in one of South Dublin's most desirable residential locations.\n\nThe property enjoys a peaceful setting with a large lawned front garden, westerly orientation to the front and a private rear garden extending to approximately 19 metres in length, offering superb space for extension and landscaping. The end-of-terrace position further enhances the appeal, providing valuable side access and additional privacy.\n\nInternally, the accommodation extends to approximately 70 sq.m. (753 sq.ft.) and comprises a welcoming entrance hall, living room, dining room, kitchen, two double bedrooms and a family bathroom.\n\nOutside\nPositioned at the very end of a quiet cul-de-sac, the house enjoys a large lawned front garden with potential, subject to planning permission, for the creation of off-street parking. The front garden benefits from a desirable westerly aspect.\n\nTo the rear lies a substantial private garden extending to approximately 19 metres (62 feet) in length and enjoying an easterly orientation. Mature planting established hedging and excellent privacy create a wonderful outdoor environment while also offering significant scope for extension, reconfiguration and landscaping.\n\nThe end-of-terrace configuration, generous side access and considerable garden depth combine to create a rare opportunity for future enhancement in a highly sought-after location.\n\nLocation\nNo. 16 enjoys an enviable position within this highly sought-after residential neighbourhood, ideally situated between the vibrant centres of Monkstown and Dún Laoghaire.\n\nResidents benefit from an exceptional range of amenities nearby, including boutique shops, artisan cafés, renowned restaurants, bars and leisure facilities. The nearby seafront offers beautiful coastal walks, swimming, sailing and a variety of marine recreational activities.\nThe area is particularly well regarded for its excellent educational facilities, with a number of highly respected primary and secondary schools within easy reach, including Monkstown Educate Together and CBC Monkstown.\n\nTransport links are excellent. The E1, E2, 7, 7A and S8 bus routes are all readily accessible, while Salthill & Monkstown DART Station is approximately a ten-minute walk away, providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre and the surrounding coastal suburbs."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nReception Hall - 3.3m x 2m\nWelcoming entrance hall with laminate flooring, electric heating, fuse board, electricity meter and understairs storage.\n\nSitting Room - 4m x 2.5m\nFront-facing reception room featuring a picture rail and original fireplace with electric inset, creating a cosy focal point.\n\nRear Lobby - \n\n\nBreakfast/Dining Room - 4m x 3.2m\nA spacious dining room overlooking the rear garden, complete with an original fireplace, laminate flooring and storage press.\n\nKitchen - 2m x 1.8m\nFitted with a range of units, sink unit and freestanding Beko oven. Tiled flooring and direct access to the rear garden.\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nLanding - 1m x 1.5m\nWith access hatch to the attic.\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.7m x 5.2m\nA generous double bedroom to the front with two windows, original fireplace and built-in storage closet.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.5m x 2.7m\nDouble bedroom overlooking the rear garden with two fitted wardrobes.\n\nBathroom - 1.8m x 2m\nComprising bath, wash hand basin, WC and opaque rear-facing window. Tiled flooring.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Features</li><li> End-of-terrace residence in a quiet cul-de-sac</li><li> Approx. 70 sq.m. / 753 sq.ft. accommodation</li><li> Two double bedrooms</li><li> Large front garden with potential for off-street parking (subject to planning permission)</li><li> Excellent side access</li><li> Private rear garden approximately 19 metres in length</li><li> Significant potential to extend (subject to planning permission)</li><li> Westerly front aspect and easterly rear aspect</li><li> Mature gardens and established planting</li><li> Walking distance to Monkstown and Dún Laoghaire</li><li> Approx. 10-minute walk to Salthill & Monkstown DART Station</li><li> Close to excellent schools, shops, cafés and coastal amenities</li><li> Highly sought-after South Dublin location</ul>"
      },
